1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,949
A site often has to react when an account is created, when the

2
00:00:04,949 --> 00:00:08,142
roles of a user change, or when someone signs in.

3
00:00:08,142 --> 00:00:11,452
Workflows can start from each of these user events.

4
00:00:11,452 --> 00:00:14,820
In this video, you'll build a workflow for each one.

5
00:00:19,420 --> 00:00:22,859
The Users module provides events for Workflows.

6
00:00:22,859 --> 00:00:29,281
User Created Event runs when an account is created, by an administrator or by a registration.

7
00:00:29,281 --> 00:00:35,380
User Updated Event runs whenever an account is saved, for example when its roles change.

8
00:00:36,130 --> 00:00:41,651
User Confirmed Event runs when someone follows the link in a confirmation email.

9
00:00:41,651 --> 00:00:46,787
User Enabled Event, User Disabled Event and User Deleted Event run when an

10
00:00:46,787 --> 00:00:49,740
account is enabled, disabled or deleted.

11
00:00:50,490 --> 00:00:55,152
User Loggedin Event and User Loggedout Event follow the sessions of a user.

12
00:00:55,152 --> 00:00:58,605
Both pass the user name and the roles to the workflow.

13
00:00:58,605 --> 00:01:04,360
The sign-in event also runs for logins through an external provider, and passes that provider.

14
00:01:05,110 --> 00:01:07,867
The Users module provides three tasks.

15
00:01:07,867 --> 00:01:12,128
Assign User Role Task adds a user to a role, and Validate User

16
00:01:12,128 --> 00:01:16,201
Task checks whether the visitor is signed in and in a role.

17
00:01:16,201 --> 00:01:21,840
Register User Task creates an account from form fields, and needs the Email feature.

18
00:01:26,140 --> 00:01:32,058
When the Workflows feature is enabled, Design, Workflows lists the workflows of the site.

19
00:01:32,058 --> 00:01:38,600
Select Create Workflow, enter Account created as the name, and select Create and open the designer.

20
00:01:39,084 --> 00:01:41,671
An empty workflow starts with an event.

21
00:01:41,671 --> 00:01:43,511
Select User Created Event.

22
00:01:43,511 --> 00:01:48,224
The designer adds it as the start activity, and marks it with a Start badge.

23
00:01:48,684 --> 00:01:53,577
Select the Done outcome of the event, search for notify, and pick Notify Task.

24
00:01:53,577 --> 00:01:57,014
The designer adds it to the right, already connected.

25
00:01:57,477 --> 00:02:02,988
A Notify Task shows a message to the person whose action started the workflow.

26
00:02:02,988 --> 00:02:09,287
Set Notification Type to Information, and enter A user account was created as the Message.

27
00:02:09,739 --> 00:02:11,076
Select Publish.

28
00:02:11,076 --> 00:02:17,249
The designer saves a draft as you work, but only the published workflow responds to events.

29
00:02:21,549 --> 00:02:24,803
Let's trigger the event by creating a user.

30
00:02:24,803 --> 00:02:28,389
Open Access Control, Users, and select Add User.

31
00:02:28,854 --> 00:02:34,104
Enter jamie.chen as the user name, and an email address at example.com.

32
00:02:34,104 --> 00:02:40,034
Select Generate password, which fills both password fields, and then select Save.

33
00:02:40,491 --> 00:02:44,196
The Users list returns with the notification from the workflow:

34
00:02:44,196 --> 00:02:45,968
A user account was created.

35
00:02:45,968 --> 00:02:49,511
The event started the workflow when the account was created.

36
00:02:53,811 --> 00:03:00,751
Back in Design, Workflows, create a second workflow named Role changed, and open the designer.

37
00:03:01,205 --> 00:03:06,442
Search the Activities pane for user updated, and select the User Updated card.

38
00:03:06,442 --> 00:03:10,495
The designer adds User Updated Event as the start activity.

39
00:03:10,954 --> 00:03:14,660
Add a Notify Task after the Done outcome, as before.

40
00:03:14,660 --> 00:03:20,794
Set Notification Type to Information, and enter A user account was updated as the Message.

41
00:03:21,245 --> 00:03:25,585
Select Publish, and the workflow responds to its event from then on.

42
00:03:26,048 --> 00:03:30,100
In Access Control, Users, select Edit for jamie.chen.

43
00:03:30,100 --> 00:03:35,388
The Roles list is part of the account, so check Editor and select Save.

44
00:03:35,853 --> 00:03:39,916
The Users list returns with the notification from the workflow.

45
00:03:39,916 --> 00:03:44,273
The role change saved the account, so User Updated Event started it.

46
00:03:48,573 --> 00:03:55,033
In Design, Workflows, create a third workflow named Welcome back, and open the designer.

47
00:03:56,262 --> 00:04:01,171
Search the Activities pane for loggedin, and select the User Logged in card.

48
00:04:01,171 --> 00:04:05,122
The designer adds User Loggedin Event as the start activity.

49
00:04:05,588 --> 00:04:08,656
Add a Notify Task after the Done outcome.

50
00:04:08,656 --> 00:04:14,008
Set Notification Type to Information, and enter Welcome back as the Message.

51
00:04:18,615 --> 00:04:19,763
Select Publish.

52
00:04:19,763 --> 00:04:23,263
Then open the user menu in the top bar and select Log off,

53
00:04:23,263 --> 00:04:24,685
which signs you out.

54
00:04:25,150 --> 00:04:26,732
Log in again as admin.

55
00:04:26,732 --> 00:04:32,046
When the sign-in succeeds, User Loggedin Event starts the workflow, and its notification

56
00:04:32,046 --> 00:04:34,250
appears on the page that follows.

57
00:04:38,550 --> 00:04:41,413
On the Workflows list, select Instances.

58
00:04:41,413 --> 00:04:46,703
Each run of a workflow is an instance, listed with its workflow and its status.

59
00:04:46,703 --> 00:04:49,130
Here, every instance is Finished.

60
00:04:49,582 --> 00:04:50,952
Open an instance.

61
00:04:50,952 --> 00:04:56,192
The read-only designer highlights the activities it ran, and the Correlation ID is

62
00:04:56,192 --> 00:04:58,872
the ID of the user the event was about.

63
00:05:00,872 --> 00:05:05,574
The user events of the Users module let a workflow react to registrations,

64
00:05:05,574 --> 00:05:07,454
role changes and sign-ins.

65
00:05:07,454 --> 00:05:08,982
Thanks for watching.

